SHA256: 551c148f7fa93dea5e537ed2dbd1e6fb96e4153dcb141a5798409691eff6d5af
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: ALSA UCM profile and mixer routing for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 ALSA Use Case Manager profile for the q6apm/AudioReach sound card of the
 OnePlus Pad 3 (card "OnePlus-Pad3-erhai-24976", driver sm8750).
 .
 The HiFi verb wires the MultiMedia front-ends to their back-ends
 (MM1 -> SECONDARY_MI2S_RX speaker TDM, MM2 -> DisplayPort, MM3 -> headset
 mic via TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3, MM4 -> internal DMICs via VA_CODEC_DMA_TX_0) and
 un-mutes the six AW88261 speaker amps.
 .
 Installing this package is all audio needs on the erhai image: PipeWire /
 WirePlumber's ACP layer resolves the profile through
 /usr/share/alsa/ucm2/conf.d/sm8750/ and applies the HiFi verb (and its
 EnableSequence mixer writes) automatically when the desktop session starts.
 .
 A USB-C monitor that carries audio gets a selectable "DisplayPort" output
 via the jack-gated UCM device; erhai-dp-audio-sync.service (triggered by a
 udev rule on DRM connector changes) bounces WirePlumber when a monitor is
 attached after boot, so the DP output appears without a manual restart.
 .
 The LPASS audio devices (lpass-lpi-pinctrl@7760000, rx/tx/va macros, both
 SoundWire masters) can end up never probed when their kernel modules load
 after the platform devices are created (late udev coldplug), which leaves
 the snd-sc8280xp machine driver without its codec components and no sound
 card at all. This package therefore also ships
 erhai-audio-bringup.service (oneshot at boot): it binds the LPI pinctrl,
 re-runs the ASoC module probe chain if needed, waits for card0 and applies
 the HiFi verb.
 .
 WirePlumber's ACP opens the UCM with the ALSA card ID ("OnePlusPad3") rather
 than "hw:0"; ALSA's UCM resolver does not match the card ID against the
 card's driver/name/longname fields, so the conf.d/ lookup misses and no ctl
 is opened (leaving ${CardId} undefined and the verb's mixer writes without a
 cdev). This package therefore also ships a legacy-path fallback
 (usr/share/alsa/ucm2/OnePlusPad3/) with a self-contained HiFi verb that
 hardcodes card 0 and opens its own control device via "cdev hw:0".

